    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all tests green.\n\nI implemented the rule by mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerEmailUnique.java`** \u2014 runs in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline after `ValidateOwnerFields`. Email is optional (skips when absent); it normalizes both the request email and each stored owner's email to lower case via the shared `OwnerEmail#normalize` rule, and throws `OwnerEmailInUseException` on a match.\n- **`OwnerEmailInUseException.java`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- **`OwnerEmailInUseExceptionHandler.java`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds **409 Conflict**.\n- Wired `checkEmail` into `owners.POST.yml` between `checkTelephone` and `checkHousehold`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\nThe new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test and the full suite both pass.",
