    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a precise, idiomatic mirror of the pre-existing `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` feature family, which is exactly the right template for a sibling uniqueness check.\n\n- **Logic in the right unit.** The check is its own function class with a single `service` method, following the per-step-one-class convention in AGENTS.md. The exception is a separate checked type, the responder is a separate handler, and the escalation is wired through YAML \u2014 matching the telephone/household/city variants already in this package.\n- **No duplication.** It correctly reuses the already-shared `OwnerEmail.normalize` rule rather than re-implementing lower-casing inline. `OwnerEmail` was explicitly built (mirroring `OwnerTelephone`) as the single source of truth shared with `ValidateOwnerFields`, so comparison here can't drift from validation. Good reuse rather than a copy.\n- **No catch-all.** Nothing is bolted onto an existing class; each concern is its own small unit, consistent with the surrounding files.\n- **YAML wiring is idiomatic.** `checkEmail` is inserted between `checkTelephone` and `checkHousehold` with `govern: [ transaction ]` and `next:`, consistent with every neighboring check step.\n- **Docs match the house style.** The Javadoc cross-references (`@link ValidateOwnerFields`, `BuildOwner`, the shared rule, the 409 handler) read exactly like the telephone equivalent a maintainer would expect.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this entirely natural \u2014 it's indistinguishable in shape from the adjacent, established uniqueness checks.",
